# Spec Navigation — What to Read for What Task

`ORCHESTRATOR_SPEC.md` is long. Read only the sections relevant to the
current task. Do not read the full spec on every request.

## Task → Spec sections

Editing writing_subagent or consequence_subagent:
  §9.4 Writing Subagent Skills (full)
  §9.5 Consequence Subagent Skills (full)
  §8 Skill Design Philosophy (§8.1–§8.5) — include §8.5 subgraphs vs monolithic prompts

Implementing resolution_subagent:
  §14 Contradiction Detection and Resolution Flow
  §7 Tool Access Matrix (resolution_subagent row)
  §5.3 Quality gate decision tree (blocked status handling)

Editing brain.py or brain.md:
  §5 Brain Node (full)
  §6 Routing Function
  §13.15 simultaneous_events forwarding

Wiring orchestrator.py:
  §3 Graph Topology
  §6 Routing Function
  §15 Checkpointer Architecture

Debugging KG queries:
  §7 Tool Access Matrix
  §13.6 Chapter sort ordering
  §13.7 as_of_chapter parameter
  §13.9 Logical ID consistency

Writing or fixing tests:
  §11.1 Novel bootstrap flow (Phase 6 bootstrap test)
  §11.2 Standard scene cycle (Phase 6 scene test)
  §12 Story State Record Lifecycle (which nodes exist when)

Checking what records a skill should produce:
  §12 Story State Record Lifecycle (the full table)

Checking brain routing After a specific worker:
  §9.1–§9.5 — the "Brain routing after" row for each skill

Checking what context keys a worker expects:
  §9.1–§9.5 — the "Key context keys" row for each skill

